<!-- 
| Feature/Gaps           | Status    | Technical Observation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| **Register Map**       | **FULL**  | Populated strictly according to `emac_reg.h`. Registers cover MAC configuration, MDIO/MII Management, and Address Filtering.                                                                                                                                                          |
| **Base Address**       | Explicit  | 0x20070000.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
| **BD Management**      | **Updated**| `TX_BD_NUM` (0x20) now includes hardware read-only pointers `TXBDPTR` and `RXBDPTR` which track the internal DMA's progress through the descriptor ring.                                                                                                                            |
| **Address Handling**   | **Fixed** | Replaced the generic `mac_address[%s]` array with specific `MAC_ADDR0` (0x40) and `MAC_ADDR1` (0x44) registers as defined in the hardware structs. Added `HASH0_ADDR` and `HASH1_ADDR` for multicast filtering.                                                                      |
| **Collision Config**   | **FULL**  | Added `COLLCONFIG` (0x1C) defining the collision valid window and maximum retries.                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| **Flow Control**       | **FULL**  | Added `TXCTRL` (0x50) for PAUSE frame timer values and manual pause requests.                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
| **Reset Values**       | **FULL**  | Reset values integrated (e.g., `MODE` resets with `BRO`, `CRCEN`, and `PAD` enabled by default; `MIIMODE` defaults to 0x64 divider).                                                                                                                                                   |
-->
